        "original_id": "abfc36e7-9b60-5611-9b99-525a7562852d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Julius Jackson, Julian Jackson, John Jackson, Tabarie Henry, LaVerne Jones-Ferrette, Thomas Barrows III, Ned Gerard, Josh Laban\n- Events: 2008 Summer Olympics\n- Places: U.S. Virgin Islands, Beijing, Puerto Rico, Mexico\n- Species: Pilosocereus robinii\n\nFacts:\n- Julian Jackson was born on September 12, 1960, and he is a former professional boxer from the U.S. Virgin Islands who competed from 1981 to 1998.\n- Julius Jackson is the son of boxer Julian Jackson.\n- At the 2008 Summer Olympics in Beijing, seven athletes represented the Virgin Islands: Tabarie Henry and LaVerne Jones-Ferrette in track and field, John and Julius Jackson in boxing, Thomas Barrows III in sailing, Ned Gerard in shooting, and Josh Laban in swimming.\n- Pilosocereus robinii has been reported from Puerto Rico, the Virgin Islands, and Mexico.",
